{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"What Predicts Repayment Difficulty?\"\n",
        "subtitle: \"Default-Rate Driver Scan · Home Credit application data\"\n",
        "author: \"Chuch\"\n",
        "date: today\n",
        "date-format: \"MMMM YYYY\"\n",
        "format:\n",
        "  revealjs:\n",
        "    theme: [default, brand.scss]\n",
        "    slide-number: c/t\n",
        "    transition: fade\n",
        "    transition-speed: fast\n",
        "    width: 1280\n",
        "    height: 720\n",
        "    center: false\n",
        "    menu: false\n",
        "    progress: false\n",
        "    auto-stretch: false\n",
        "    fig-align: center\n",
        "    echo: false\n",
        "    embed-resources: true\n",
        "    footer: \"Default-Rate Driver Scan · Home Credit Default Data\"\n",
        "title-slide-attributes:\n",
        "    data-background-color: \"#3D2E4F\"\n",
        "    data-background-gradient: \"radial-gradient(120% 135% at 12% 4%, #5C4577 0%, #3D2E4F 52%, #2C2039 100%)\"\n",
        "execute:\n",
        "  warning: false\n",
        "  message: false\n",
        "  freeze: auto\n",
        "jupyter: python3\n",
        "---"
      ],
      "id": "55e4cb50"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: setup\n",
        "#| include: false\n",
        "import os, sys, warnings\n",
        "warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\n",
        "import numpy as np, pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import matplotlib.ticker as mticker\n",
        "\n",
        "def find_repo_root(start, name=\"CreditRiskLearning\"):\n",
        "    p = os.path.abspath(start)\n",
        "    while True:\n",
        "        if os.path.basename(p) == name:\n",
        "            return p\n",
        "        parent = os.path.dirname(p)\n",
        "        if parent == p:\n",
        "            raise FileNotFoundError(name)\n",
        "        p = parent\n",
        "\n",
        "REPO = find_repo_root(os.getcwd())\n",
        "sys.path.append(os.path.join(REPO, \"Core Resources\"))\n",
        "sys.path.append(os.path.join(REPO, \"Core Resources\", \"Scripts\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "# Brand chart system + shared deck helpers (see Core Resources/Scripts/deck_utils.py)\n",
        "from python_style_util import p, f, s, C\n",
        "from credit_utils.eda import default_rate_by_bin\n",
        "from deck_utils import (deck_style, BRAND_RAMP, add_baseline,\n",
        "                        strip_bar_labels, small_labels, reset_labels)\n",
        "deck_style()\n",
        "\n",
        "DATA = os.path.join(REPO, \"Datasets\", \"Home Credit Default Risk\", \"application_train.csv\")\n",
        "usecols = [\"TARGET\", \"EXT_SOURCE_1\", \"EXT_SOURCE_2\", \"EXT_SOURCE_3\",\n",
        "           \"DAYS_BIRTH\", \"DAYS_EMPLOYED\", \"NAME_EDUCATION_TYPE\",\n",
        "           \"AMT_INCOME_TOTAL\", \"AMT_CREDIT\", \"AMT_ANNUITY\", \"AMT_GOODS_PRICE\", \"CODE_GENDER\"]\n",
        "df = pd.read_csv(DATA, usecols=usecols)\n",
        "df = df[df[\"CODE_GENDER\"] != \"XNA\"]\n",
        "df[\"DAYS_EMPLOYED\"] = df[\"DAYS_EMPLOYED\"].replace(365243, np.nan)\n",
        "df[\"AGE_YEARS\"] = -df[\"DAYS_BIRTH\"] / 365.25\n",
        "df[\"EMP_YEARS\"] = -df[\"DAYS_EMPLOYED\"] / 365.25\n",
        "\n",
        "def _sd(n, d): return n / d.replace(0, np.nan)\n",
        "df[\"DTI\"]          = _sd(df[\"AMT_ANNUITY\"], df[\"AMT_INCOME_TOTAL\"])\n",
        "df[\"CREDIT_GOODS\"] = _sd(df[\"AMT_CREDIT\"],  df[\"AMT_GOODS_PRICE\"])\n",
        "df[\"EMPLOYED_AGE\"] = _sd(df[\"DAYS_EMPLOYED\"], df[\"DAYS_BIRTH\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "BASE = df[\"TARGET\"].mean()\n",
        "N = len(df)"
      ],
      "id": "setup",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## The short version {.hero data-kick=\"Executive summary\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.hero-wrap}\n",
        "::: {.hero-col}\n",
        "<div class=\"hero-num\">~8%<small>of applicants hit repayment difficulty</small></div>\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.hero-col}\n",
        "Across **307,000+ applications**, a handful of signals separate that 8% cleanly:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **External credit scores** — by far the strongest\n",
        "- **Age & job tenure** — younger, less-tenured default more\n",
        "- **Affordability ratios** — repayment size *relative* to the loan\n",
        "\n",
        "And one thing that barely matters alone: **the raw loan amount**.\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.takeaway}\n",
        "This deck is the *scan* — which fields carry signal — before any model is built. Every rate is read against the **8% base rate**.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## The data in one slide {data-kick=\"The data\"}"
      ],
      "id": "8e65efa0"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "fig-width": 10,
        "fig-height": 3
      },
      "source": [
        "counts = df[\"TARGET\"].value_counts(normalize=True).sort_index()\n",
        "labels = [\"Repaid on time\", \"Repayment difficulty\"]\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(11, 3.4))\n",
        "bars = ax.barh(labels, counts.values, color=[p(\"jacaranda\", 300), p(\"gold\", 300)],\n",
        "               alpha=0.95, edgecolor=\"white\", linewidth=1.2, height=0.62)\n",
        "for b, v in zip(bars, counts.values):\n",
        "    ax.text(v + 0.012, b.get_y() + b.get_height()/2, f\"{v:.1%}\", va=\"center\",\n",
        "            fontweight=\"bold\", fontfamily=f(\"mono\"), fontsize=12, color=C.text)\n",
        "ax.set_xlim(0, 1); ax.set_xlabel(\"Share of applications\")\n",
        "ax.set_title(f\"{N:,} applications  ·  122 fields  ·  {BASE:.1%} hit repayment difficulty\",\n",
        "             loc=\"left\")\n",
        "ax.grid(axis=\"x\"); ax.grid(axis=\"y\", visible=False)\n",
        "ax.invert_yaxis()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "13d1292a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.takeaway}\n",
        "The classes are **imbalanced** — roughly 12 good for every 1 bad. That's normal for credit, and it's why every group is read against the 8% line rather than a 50/50 split.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## How to read a driver {data-kick=\"Method\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "For each field we sort applicants into bins (low → high) and check the **default rate in each bin** against the 8% base line.\n",
        "\n",
        "- Bars that **slope** — the field separates good from bad → useful signal.\n",
        "- Bars that stay **flat** on the line — no signal → drop it.\n",
        "\n",
        "Colour just re-states height: [lighter = safer]{.stat}, the [deeper the purple]{.stat}, the higher the default rate.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.takeaway}\n",
        "That's the whole method. The next slides are this one chart, one field at a time.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Strongest signal — external credit scores {data-kick=\"Signal · strongest\"}"
      ],
      "id": "533b9a98"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "fig-width": 11,
        "fig-height": 4.3
      },
      "source": [
        "fig, axes = default_rate_by_bin(\n",
        "    df, [\"EXT_SOURCE_2\", \"EXT_SOURCE_3\", \"EXT_SOURCE_1\"],\n",
        "    target=\"TARGET\", ncols=3, bins=10, bin_label=\"rank\",\n",
        "    grade_scale=BRAND_RAMP, na_as_bin=True, panel_w=5.0, panel_h=4.7,\n",
        "    show_base_rate=False,\n",
        ")\n",
        "add_baseline(axes, BASE)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "57e17f0c",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.takeaway}\n",
        "A clean, steep slide from **~20% default in the lowest-score bin to ~2–3% in the highest**. These pre-built external scores are the single best predictors in the data.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Age & job tenure {data-kick=\"Signal · demographics\"}"
      ],
      "id": "9368fe7a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "fig-width": 10.5,
        "fig-height": 4.2
      },
      "source": [
        "fig, axes = default_rate_by_bin(\n",
        "    df, [\"AGE_YEARS\", \"EMP_YEARS\"], target=\"TARGET\",\n",
        "    ncols=2, bins=8, method=\"quantile\", bin_label=\"range\",\n",
        "    grade_scale=BRAND_RAMP, na_as_bin=True, panel_w=6.4, panel_h=4.7,\n",
        "    show_base_rate=False,\n",
        ")\n",
        "add_baseline(axes, BASE)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "0e1a88f4",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.takeaway}\n",
        "Both slope the intuitive way: **younger applicants, and those with less time in a job, default more**. Stability reads as lower risk. (The \"missing\" tenure bar is pensioners — correctly low-risk.)\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Education tells a clean story too {data-kick=\"Signal · education\"}"
      ],
      "id": "41abcf7a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "fig-width": 10,
        "fig-height": 3.7
      },
      "source": [
        "order = df.groupby(\"NAME_EDUCATION_TYPE\")[\"TARGET\"].mean().sort_values()\n",
        "from matplotlib import colors as _mc\n",
        "norm = _mc.Normalize(order.min(), order.max())\n",
        "rgba = BRAND_RAMP(norm(order.values)); rgba[:, 3] = 0.95\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(11, 4.2))\n",
        "bars = ax.barh(order.index.astype(str), order.values, color=rgba,\n",
        "               edgecolor=\"white\", linewidth=1.0)\n",
        "ax.axvline(BASE, ls=\"--\", color=C.text_muted, lw=1, zorder=1.4)\n",
        "ax.text(BASE, len(order)-0.35, f\" base {BASE:.1%}\", va=\"bottom\", ha=\"left\",\n",
        "        fontsize=11, color=C.text_muted, fontfamily=f(\"mono\"), zorder=5,\n",
        "        bbox=dict(facecolor=\"white\", edgecolor=\"none\", boxstyle=\"round,pad=0.18\", alpha=0.85))\n",
        "for b, v in zip(bars, order.values):\n",
        "    ax.text(v + 0.002, b.get_y()+b.get_height()/2, f\"{v:.1%}\", va=\"center\",\n",
        "            fontweight=\"bold\", fontsize=12, fontfamily=f(\"mono\"), color=C.text)\n",
        "ax.set_xlim(0, order.values.max() * 1.16)   # headroom so the top % label never clips\n",
        "ax.xaxis.set_major_formatter(mticker.PercentFormatter(xmax=1))\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Default rate by education level\", loc=\"left\")\n",
        "ax.grid(axis=\"x\"); ax.grid(axis=\"y\", visible=False)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "b260e08f",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.takeaway}\n",
        "A steady gradient from **higher education (~2%) to lower secondary (~11%)** — education is a real, ordered driver.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## The surprise — loan amounts barely matter {data-kick=\"Signal · the surprise\"}"
      ],
      "id": "024b273a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "fig-width": 11,
        "fig-height": 4.3
      },
      "source": [
        "small_labels(9)   # denser bins -> smaller per-bar labels so they never touch\n",
        "fig, axes = default_rate_by_bin(\n",
        "    df, [\"AMT_CREDIT\", \"AMT_INCOME_TOTAL\", \"AMT_ANNUITY\"],\n",
        "    target=\"TARGET\", ncols=3, bins=10, bin_label=\"rank\",\n",
        "    grade_scale=BRAND_RAMP, panel_w=5.0, panel_h=4.7, show_base_rate=False,\n",
        ")\n",
        "reset_labels()\n",
        "add_baseline(axes, BASE)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "477f7ad3",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.caveat}\n",
        "As **raw amounts**, these are nearly flat — a big loan is not, by itself, a risky loan. The signal isn't the size; it's the size *relative* to income and the asset. That motivates the engineered ratios.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Engineered affordability ratios {data-kick=\"Feature engineering\"}"
      ],
      "id": "36f24aea"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "fig-width": 11,
        "fig-height": 4.3
      },
      "source": [
        "fig, axes = default_rate_by_bin(\n",
        "    df, [\"EMPLOYED_AGE\", \"CREDIT_GOODS\", \"DTI\"], target=\"TARGET\",\n",
        "    ncols=3, bins=12, bin_label=\"rank\", grade_scale=BRAND_RAMP, na_as_bin=True,\n",
        "    panel_w=5.0, panel_h=4.7, show_base_rate=False,\n",
        ")\n",
        "strip_bar_labels(axes)   # 12 near-equal bins -> labels collide; let the y-axis carry values\n",
        "for ax in np.ravel(np.asarray(axes)):\n",
        "    ax.margins(y=0.06)\n",
        "add_baseline(axes, BASE)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "dd89abaf",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.caveat}\n",
        "**Job-tenure share** and **loan-to-value** (`CREDIT_GOODS`) slope cleanly — the affordability signal the raw amounts lacked. But **debt-to-income (`DTI`) is flat**: the textbook metric underperforms here, almost certainly because self-reported income is noisy.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## What we carry forward {data-kick=\"Shortlist\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "**Retained** as candidate drivers for the modelling screen:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **External scores** (strongest), **age & tenure**, **education**\n",
        "- **Affordability ratios** — loan-to-value and tenure-share\n",
        "- Weak-but-documented: DTI / income ratios (kept to *show* they underperform)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Deliberately parked** (reversible, one line to re-add):\n",
        "\n",
        "- Social-circle and bureau-enquiry counts — too weak to earn a baseline slot\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.takeaway}\n",
        "A **lean, defensible shortlist** beats a kitchen sink — it's the judgment call, not the field count, that matters.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Caveats & what's next {data-kick=\"Caveats · next\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Gender is excluded** from any model — responsible-lending / anti-discrimination — and used for context only.\n",
        "- The model **leans heavily on opaque external scores**; self-reported income is noisy.\n",
        "- Application-time data only; **missing values are kept as their own group** where the absence is itself informative.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.caveat}\n",
        "**Next:** turn this scan into a ranked screen (WOE / Information Value), then a first interpretable scorecard. This deck answers *\"what looks predictive\"*; the next answers *\"how strongly, and in what order.\"*\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## {.closing background-color=\"#3D2E4F\" background-gradient=\"radial-gradient(120% 135% at 88% 96%, #5C4577 0%, #3D2E4F 52%, #2C2039 100%)\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "<div class=\"rule\"></div>\n",
        "<div class=\"lead\">From scan to scorecard.</div>\n",
        "<div class=\"sub\">This deck answered <em>what looks predictive</em>. Next: rank every driver by Information Value, then build a first interpretable, leakage-safe scorecard.</div>\n",
        "<div class=\"tag\">Default-Rate Driver Scan · Home Credit · Flagship PD Model</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "```{=html}\n",
        "<script>\n",
        "window.addEventListener('load', () => {\n",
        "  const t = document.getElementById('title-slide');\n",
        "  if (t && !t.querySelector('.cover-meta')) {\n",
        "    // header: kicker + gold rule, prepended above the title\n",
        "    const head = document.createElement('div');\n",
        "    head.className = 'cover-head';\n",
        "    head.innerHTML = '<div class=\"cover-kick\">01 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Default-Rate Driver Scan</div><div class=\"cover-rule\"></div>';\n",
        "    t.insertBefore(head, t.firstChild);\n",
        "    // stat chips, appended below the author line\n",
        "    const d = document.createElement('div');\n",
        "    d.className = 'cover-meta';\n",
        "    d.innerHTML = `\n",
        "      <div class=\"cm\"><span class=\"cm-n\">307,511</span><span class=\"cm-l\">Applications</span></div>\n",
        "      <div class=\"cm\"><span class=\"cm-n\">122</span><span class=\"cm-l\">Raw fields</span></div>\n",
        "      <div class=\"cm\"><span class=\"cm-n\">8.1%</span><span class=\"cm-l\">Base default rate</span></div>\n",
        "      <div class=\"cm\"><span class=\"cm-n\">11</span><span class=\"cm-l\">Drivers screened</span></div>`;\n",
        "    t.appendChild(d);\n",
        "  }\n",
        "});\n",
        "</script>\n",
        "```"
      ],
      "id": "72323256"
    }
  ],
